    "result_text": "Green. Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec adds a `bulkSignupWarning` flag: `true` once more than 80 owners share a signup day, else `false`. In this codebase every business rule lives on `POST /api/owners` and is read back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`, and derived owner fields surface through `OwnerDto`.\n\nI kept structural impact low by computing the flag at response time (like the daily-limit rule counts) rather than adding a persisted column \u2014 which would have meant editing the large `Owner` entity, the mapper, and four dialect `schema.sql` files. Changes:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the readOnly `bulkSignupWarning` boolean to the `Owner` schema (regenerates `OwnerDto` with `setBulkSignupWarning`).\n2. **`BulkSignup.java`** (new) \u2014 a tiny stateless helper (`warned(owner, repo)`) counting owners registered on the owner's day against the threshold of 80. Mirrors `EnsureDailyLimit`'s accumulation path.\n3. **`RespondWithOwner.java`** (GET responder) \u2014 set the flag on the DTO before sending.\n4. **`RespondWithOwnerCreated.java`** (POST responder) \u2014 same, so the create response carries it too.\n\nEvery touched function is a single-method class (WMC_other \u2248 0) with a one- or two-line change; no existing method or class grew. The counting logic sits in one cohesive new unit reused by both responders. `AcceptanceTest` passes (1/1, BUILD SUCCESS).",
